Description: open-source vector illustration editor
 VectorCraft is a native vector illustration app written in Rust. It has pen,
 shape and brush tools, artboards, type, gradients, symbols and live effects,
 and opens and saves SVG and PDF. It renders on the GPU (wgpu).
 .
 The headless converter, command runner and MCP server that drive the same
 editor commands are in the storytold-vectorcraft-cli package.

Package: storytold-vectorcraft-cli
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
Suggests: storytold-vectorcraft (= ${binary:Version}),
         storytold-craft-fonts,
Enhances: storytold-vectorcraft,
Description: headless command runner and MCP server for the VectorCraft editor
 vectorcraft-cli runs VectorCraft's editor commands without a window: it
 converts and inspects vector files (SVG, PDF and the other formats the editor
 opens), runs the editor's commands from a list or a script and renders the
 result.
 .
 vectorcraft-cli mcp starts an MCP server on standard input and output, so that
 an AI agent can drive the editor engine, headless or attached to a running
 VectorCraft window, and see the result as an image. It has no windowing or GPU
 dependencies. The storytold-vectorcraft package provides the editor window.
